# Authors: Davide Batic and Dr. Denys Dutykh (Mathematics Department, Khalifa University
# of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE)
#
# Citation metadata in Citation File Format 1.2.0, from which GitHub draws its button
# "Cite this repository". The article that these codes accompany has been submitted and
# has no public record yet, so the software itself is cited.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes or their results, please cite this software as given below."
title: "kerr-dirac-scattering: two-channel Dollard scattering and partial-wave resonances for massive Dirac fields on Kerr"
abstract: >-
  Python codes accompanying the article "Two-Channel Dollard Scattering and Partial-Wave
  Resonances for Massive Dirac Fields on Kerr" by D. Batic and D. Dutykh. They compute the
  partial scattering matrices of massive Dirac fields outside Schwarzschild and Kerr black
  holes by matching Jost solutions of the radial system, check unitarity, the conservation of
  the Wronskian and the identities implied by the conjugation symmetry, follow the convergence
  in the outer endpoint, and locate the quasi-bound levels in the mass gap with their
  parameter-free Breit-Wigner signature and a count of zeros by the argument principle.
type: software
